      "ogTitle": "George Washington — Historical Profile",
      "ogDescription": "Primer presidente de United States y comandante del Ejército Continental, retratado en el banknote de One Dollar, Red Seal.",
      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <header>\n    <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 0;\">\n      <a href=\"/en/collection/colonial-paper-money/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em;\">&larr; Colonial coin catalog</a>\n    </nav>\n  </header>\n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/colonial-paper-money/profile-george-washington/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:24px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center;\">\n\n        <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:720px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n          <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">Historical Profile &middot; United States</span>\n          <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px); line-height:1.1; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">George Washington</h1>\n          <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">Westmoreland, 1732 &mdash; Mount Vernon, 1799</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:400px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 56px;\">\n          <div style=\"width:100%; aspect-ratio:960/1166; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); overflow:hidden;\">\n            <picture style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:100%;\">\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/washington-portrait-stuart-480.webp 480w, /uploads/washington-portrait-stuart.webp 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 448px) calc(100vw - 48px), 400px\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img src=\"/uploads/washington-portrait-stuart.jpg\" alt=\"Oil portrait of George Washington, in a black coat and white ruffled shirt\" width=\"960\" height=\"1166\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;\">\n            </picture>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; font-style:italic;\">\n            <span style=\"display:block;\">George Washington</span>\n            <span style=\"display:block;\">By Gilbert Stuart &mdash;<a href=\"https://www.clarkart.edu/ArtPiece/Detail/George-Washington\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Clark Art Institute<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px;\">\n          <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Birth</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">February 22, 1732 &mdash; Westmoreland County, Virginia</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Death</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">December 14, 1799 &mdash; Mount Vernon, Virginia</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Key Role</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Commander in Chief of the Continental Army (1775&ndash;1783) and first president of the United States (1789&ndash;1797)</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">1. The Commander of Independence</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\">A Virginia landowner and soldier with experience in the French and Indian War, Washington was appointed commander in chief of the newly created Continental Army by the Second Continental Congress in 1775, when the War of Independence against Great Britain broke out.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">Despite numerous initial defeats, his consistent leadership through the harsh winters of Valley Forge and his decisive victory at Yorktown (1781), with French support, sealed American independence in 1783.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">2. The First President</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\">Unanimously elected as the first president under the new Constitution, Washington established numerous institutional precedents that endure today: the advisory cabinet, the informal two-term limit, and the tradition of the farewell address.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">He voluntarily relinquished power in 1797, an exceptional gesture at the time that strengthened the young nation's republican character in contrast to European monarchical models.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">3. Numismatic Legacy</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">Washington's portrait is the most reproduced in the history of American paper money: it appears on the<a href=\"/en/collection/one-dollar-red-seal-1928/\">One Dollar, Red Seal (1928)</a>from this collection, as well as on the current one dollar bill from 1869 to the present.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <div style=\"margin-top:44px; padding-top:20px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 10px; font-style:normal;\">Notes</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0;\">Biography based on standard historical sources about the American Revolutionary War and the presidency of George Washington.</p>\n          </div>\n\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
